  ],
  "text": "The biggest environmental disaster of the eighties is on track to be gone by twenty sixty six. Ozone is a thin layer of gas that soaks up the ultraviolet in sunlight. Then fridges and hairspray started leaking chemicals that tore it apart. By nineteen eighty five, the hole over Antarctica was wider than a continent. Then something almost unheard of happened. Every country on Earth signed the same ban. It worked because the fix was cheap. Swap one chemical for another one. And only a handful of factories made the stuff, so the ban had somewhere to land. So this is not proof that we always fix things. It is proof that we can when it is easy. The hole is measurably smaller now. We do not get to say that very often. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
